      "n3"
     ],
     "depends_on": [],
     "hidden": false,
     "text": "What was made and why: Why Al2O3-YSZ thermal barrier coatings fail sooner -> Add Al2O3 to the YSZ top coat (Al2O3-YSZ) and comp -> Plasma spraying of YSZ and Al2O3-YSZ coatings"
    },
    {
     "step": 2,
     "role": "read",
     "nodes": [
      "o1"
     ],
     "depends_on": [
      1
     ],
     "hidden": false,
     "text": "Open the panels F1 [XRD] and compare (compare across conditions)"
    },
    {
     "step": 3,
     "role": "observation",
     "nodes": [
      "o1"
     ],
     "depends_on": [
      2
     ],
     "hidden": true,
     "text": "Observation: YSZ pattern has a small (012) peak at ~43 deg and split peaks at ~35, 60 and 74 deg; Al2O3-YSZ pattern has neither"
    },
    {
     "step": 4,
     "role": "claim",
     "nodes": [
      "n4"
     ],
     "depends_on": [
      3
     ],
     "hidden": true,
     "text": "Claim it establishes: As-sprayed Al2O3-YSZ is cubic ZrO2, while YSZ is mainly tetragonal ZrO2 with a little cubic phase"
    },
    {
     "step": 5,
     "role": "downstream",
     "nodes": [
      "n11",
      "n12",
      "n17",
      "n20"
     ],
     "depends_on": [
      4
     ],
     "hidden": true,
     "text": "Feeds: Al2O3-YSZ undergoes a much larger micro-strain than YSZ during thermal cycling"
    }
   ]
